fresh-eyes: agent review of the merge-gate output capture. Scope: cargo test output is captured, and the last 40 lines print on failure. The reviewer exercised both paths in a sandbox with a stub cargo: the red path exits 1 and names the failing test in stderr; the green path proceeds. set -e, the stdin capture order, and </dev/null were checked adversarially. Mutation: the pre-fix state is the mutant — with >/dev/null, the sandbox red run shows no test name; with the capture, it does.
